{
  "$Comment": "A weapon of every family, unmade: one criterion per family the game ships as gear, each 'Weapon_<Family>_' on PREFIX so any grade of that family counts, and every one of the fifteen must complete. Shields are a Weapon_ family in vanilla and so are listed; the ammunition, bombs, darts and deployables that share the prefix are not gear, the tables refuse them, and they are left out. Two families are left out because no player can bring one to the table: the tribal claws (no recipe, drop, shop or chest gives them) and the guns (every Weapon_Gun_ item is Technical quality and carried only by NPCs, and the tables' protect list refuses that quality). Neither of Update 7's new goblin weapons replaces them: the bangstick is a thrown bomb (Family Bomb), which the tables refuse, and the scrap flamethrower is only ever held by burner goblins, which never drop it, and no recipe, shop or chest gives it. Nothing in the game hands a player a wand or a blowgun either, so Enchanter Orrin's shelf sells one of each (ShopEntries/MMOSkillTree/Mmo_Enchanter_Offer_Wand.json and Mmo_Enchanter_Offer_Blowgun.json); take an offer away and its criterion can no longer be earned. A family missing from this list is simply not asked for; add a criterion to ask for one a pack introduces. Every criterion is qualified to 'Disenchanting_Table' on PREFIX, so both tables count and the Sawmill never does.",
